  "name": "SGOT (AST)- SERUM ",
  "code": "SGOT",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">​<br></span></p><ul><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the SGOT (AST) level is within the normal range, it typically indicates that the liver, heart, and muscles are functioning normally.</li><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the SGOT (AST) level is above the normal range, it may indicate liver damage, such as hepatitis or cirrhosis, heart damage, such as a heart attack, or muscle damage, such as a muscle injury or a condition called rhabdomyolysis. However, elevated SGOT (AST) levels may also be caused by other factors, such as alcohol consumption, certain medications, or strenuous exercise.</li><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the SGOT (AST) level is significantly elevated, it may indicate severe liver or heart damage, and further evaluation and treatment may be necessary.</li></ul>",
